<span id="top"></span>

<!-- ============================================================= hero -->
<section class="hero">
  <canvas id="monolith" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hero__grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="hero__in wrap wrap--wide">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">
      <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="label">Lambda Symbolics OÜ</span>
      <span class="label sep" style="color:rgba(255,254,250,.3)">/</span>
      <span class="label">v0.49.0</span>
      <span class="label sep" style="color:rgba(255,254,250,.3)">/</span>
      <span class="label">ISC licensed</span>
    </p>

    <h1 class="display d1" data-split>A programming agent that can <em>rewrite&nbsp;itself</em> while it runs.</h1>

    <p class="hero__lede" data-rv style="--d:5">
      Autolith works in your terminal and directly in your repository. It reads
      and edits files, searches, runs commands and tests, and keeps project
      context. It lives inside a Common Lisp image it can inspect, extend,
      break, and recover.
    </p>

    <div class="hero__acts" data-rv style="--d:6">
      <a class="btn" href="#install"><span>Install Autolith</span><span class="btn__arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://lambda-symbolics.com/autolith/docs"><span>Read the docs</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero__statwrap wrap wrap--wide">
  <div class="scrollcue"><span>Scroll</span><i></i></div>
  <ul class="hero__stats" data-rv="fade" style="--d:8">
    <li><b>1</b><span>process holds the agent,<br>tools, terminal and state</span></li>
    <li><b>3.1&nbsp;MB</b><span>corpus answered inside a<br>59.6&nbsp;K-token conversation</span></li>
    <li><b>6</b><span>platforms, from Linux<br>to OpenBSD to Windows</span></li>
    <li><b>0</b><span>restarts needed to change<br>the running agent</span></li>
  </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========================================================== marquee -->
<div class="band band--ink band--tight" style="padding-block:0">
  <div class="marquee">
    <div class="marquee__track" id="mq1">
      <span>Self-modifying</span><span>Append-only conversations</span><span>Recursive inference</span><span>Private image commits</span><span>Pristine recovery image</span><span>MCP</span><span>Skills</span><span>Structured-output jobs</span><span>Generations and rollback</span><span>S-expressions all the way down</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ========================================================== pillars -->
<section class="band band--paper" id="pillars">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="headwrap" style="margin-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,6vh,4.5rem)">
      <div class="head" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <p class="label label--accent">01 — What it is</p>
        <h2 class="display d2" data-split>For developers who want an agent they can <em>inspect, extend,</em> and recover.</h2>
        <p class="lede head__lede" data-rv>
          Not a wrapper around another agent process. One Common Lisp image that
          holds the provider client, the terminal, the tool registry, the MCP
          connections, the conversation store, and the code that decides what
          happens next.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="mascot shadowband" data-rv>
        <div class="mascot__bar"><span>Autolith</span><span>Resident agent</span></div>
        <div class="mascot__frame">
          <img src="autolith.png" width="998" height="897" alt="The Autolith mascot, rendered in black ink and bitmap dither on paper">
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <ol class="pillars">
      <li class="pillar" data-rv style="--d:0">
        <span class="pillar__num">01</span>
        <div><h3 class="display pillar__t">Repository&nbsp;work</h3><span class="pillar__mark">read · edit · search · run</span></div>
        <p class="pillar__body">Filesystem, shell, and search tools with visible results. Workspace search runs in-process through <a class="ulink" href="https://github.com/dmtrKovalenko/fff"><code>fff</code></a>, a fast Rust search library, with the index kept warm.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pillar" data-rv style="--d:1">
        <span class="pillar__num">02</span>
        <div><h3 class="display pillar__t">Oversized&nbsp;context</h3><span class="pillar__mark">rlm.complete</span></div>
        <p class="pillar__body">Recursive inference over corpora larger than the model window. The corpus never enters a prompt; the model drives a Lisp environment over it under a call and token budget.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pillar" data-rv style="--d:2">
        <span class="pillar__num">03</span>
        <div><h3 class="display pillar__t">Continuity</h3><span class="pillar__mark">resume · vault · generations</span></div>
        <p class="pillar__body">Portable conversations, memories, agendas, checkpoints, and recovery. Steering messages survive crashes in a conversation-scoped vault that is never resubmitted behind your back.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pillar" data-rv style="--d:3">
        <span class="pillar__num">04</span>
        <div><h3 class="display pillar__t">Live&nbsp;Lisp</h3><span class="pillar__mark">self.* · lisp.*</span></div>
        <p class="pillar__body">An SBCL runtime it can inspect, test, and extend. Named, heap-isolated workers run experiments; the active image takes changes only through a journalled transaction.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="pillar" data-rv style="--d:4">
        <span class="pillar__num">05</span>
        <div><h3 class="display pillar__t">Unattended</h3><span class="pillar__mark">run-job</span></div>
        <p class="pillar__body">A single-job boundary with a structured-output contract, drivable from scripts and CI. Data-only S-expression envelope in, trace and usage out, result installed atomically.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================= repl -->
<section class="band band--ink" id="repl" style="padding-block:0">
  <div class="scrub" id="sugarScrub" style="height:265svh">
    <div class="scrub__sticky">
      <div class="wrap wrap--wide" style="width:100%;padding-block:clamp(5rem,10vh,7rem)">
        <div class="head" style="margin-bottom:clamp(2rem,5vh,3.5rem)">
          <p class="label label--accent">02 — The prompt is the REPL</p>
          <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Messages are just <em>syntax sugar.</em></h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sugar">
          <div class="sugar__stage"><span class="sugar__glyphs" id="sugar" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sr">Hello Autolith! How do you do? desugars to (prompt :to 'autolith "Hello Autolith! How do you do?")</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sugar__steps">
            <div class="sugar__step" data-step="0">
              <h4>Prose</h4>
              <p>You type a sentence. The message window is not a text box with a send button.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="sugar__step" data-step="1">
              <h4>A call</h4>
              <p>It is a Lisp reader. Your sentence is read as a call to <code>prompt</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="sugar__step" data-step="2">
              <h4>An address</h4>
              <p>With the default argument restored. Change it and you are talking to a child instead.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap wrap--wide" style="padding-bottom:var(--band-y)">
    <div class="two">
      <div class="stack-3" data-rv>
        <h3 class="display d3">So a prompt can be&nbsp;computed.</h3>
        <p class="prose">
          Prose, callable commands, tools, and explicit Common Lisp share one
          input. A form runs in the active image and the model sees the result,
          so a prompt can be read off disk, templated, or produced by the
          program you are debugging.
        </p>
        <div class="term">
          <div class="term__bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>autolith — prompt window</span></div>
          <div class="term__body"><pre><span class="c-dim">;; a computed prompt</span>
(<span class="c-amber">prompt</span> (<span class="c-amber">read-file</span> <span class="c-jade">"review-notes.org"</span>))

<span class="c-dim">;; a tool, called by hand</span>
(<span class="c-amber">resource.read</span> <span class="c-azure">:uri</span> <span class="c-jade">"workspace:."</span>)

<span class="c-dim">;; introspection, right there</span>
(<span class="c-amber">describe</span> '<span class="c-paper">application</span>)</pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-3" data-rv style="--d:1">
        <h3 class="display d3">And you can steer any child in the&nbsp;tree.</h3>
        <p class="prose">
          When Autolith delegates work it keeps going while the children run.
          Children are addressable by name, so you can correct one mid-flight.
          Its next useful verbal response comes back to the primary terminal.
        </p>
        <div class="term">
          <div class="term__bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>autolith — children</span></div>
          <div class="term__body"><pre>(<span class="c-amber">prompt</span> <span class="c-azure">:to</span> '<span class="c-paper">test-review</span>
        <span class="c-jade">"Run the focused tests and
         report only failures."</span>)

<span class="c-dim">→ test-review  acknowledged</span>
<span class="c-dim">→ primary      still working</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ======================================================== live image -->
<section class="band band--paper" id="image">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="label label--accent">03 — The live image</p>
      <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Update the running agent <em>without restarting it.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede head__lede" data-rv>
        Autolith can inspect and replace complete functions, methods, classes,
        macros, conditions, and global settings in its running image. An
        exploratory change takes effect immediately and is recorded in an
        append-only mutation journal. It can be exercised, discarded, or
        retained as a private image commit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="two" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="stack-3">
        <p class="label">A representative mutation transaction</p>
        <div class="crash shadowband" id="crashBox" data-rv="fade">
          <div class="term term--paper" style="border:0">
            <div class="term__bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>active image · journal</span></div>
            <div class="term__body">
              <ol class="ladder" id="ladder">
                <li><span class="ar">→</span><span><b>lisp.source</b> <span class="c-dim">TERMINAL-UI--DURATION-TEXT target self</span></span></li>
                <li class="re-line"><span class="ar">←</span><span class="re">complete tracked DEFUN</span></li>
                <li><span class="ar">→</span><span><b>self.redefine</b> <span class="c-dim">(defun terminal-ui--duration-text …)</span></span></li>
                <li class="re-line"><span class="ar">←</span><span class="re">compiled and installed in the active image</span></li>
                <li><span class="ar">→</span><span><b>self.exercise</b> <span class="c-dim">(assert (string= "1d 2:00:00" …))</span></span></li>
                <li class="re-line"><span class="ar">←</span><span class="re">journalled assertion passed</span></li>
                <li><span class="ar">→</span><span><b>self.diff</b></span></li>
                <li class="re-line"><span class="ar">←</span><span class="re">one reconstructible live mutation</span></li>
                <li><span class="ar">→</span><span><b>self.commit</b> <span class="c-dim">"Show days in long durations"</span></span></li>
                <li class="re-line"><span class="ar">←</span><span class="re">private image commit · complete reconstruct.lisp retained in private Git</span></li>
              </ol>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="label" style="color:var(--dimmer)">The commit contains a manifest and a complete executable Lisp replay script. It changes the active agent without quietly patching the tracked source repository.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-3">
        <p class="label">Then break it on purpose</p>
        <p class="prose">
          The formatter above feeds the live status row, so a deliberate bad
          redefinition kills the process outright. That is the interesting case,
          and it is the one Autolith is built for.
        </p>
        <div class="recovery shadowband" id="recovery">
          <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:.9rem;color:var(--jade-deep)">Recovery image · read-only</p>
          <ul class="stack-1" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.6">
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> crash capsule <b>efa6aa16</b> written</li>
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> pristine recovery image booted</li>
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> restarted from clean committed source</li>
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> private commit re-selected</li>
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> conversation restored</li>
            <li><span style="color:var(--jade-deep)">✓</span> read-only diagnosis turn opened</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="prose" style="margin-top:1.1rem;font-size:.95rem">
            It asks before repairing anything. <strong>The committed mutation survived its own author.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="prose" style="font-size:.95rem">
          And when a signal interrupts ordinary work, the live restart debugger
          offers <em>Ask Autolith why this failed</em>: an independent diagnosis
          beside the still-live restarts, with up to three validated recovery
          proposals.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================== rlm / context -->
<section class="band band--ink" id="context">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="label label--accent">04 — Oversized context</p>
      <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Context larger than the window is an <em>environment,</em> not a prompt.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="rlm" id="rlm">
      <div class="rlm__viz" id="rlmViz" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div>
        <p class="prose">
          <code>rlm.complete</code> interns the corpus as a content-addressed
          object. The root model receives only its label, size, and digest, and
          drives a heap-isolated Lisp environment through bounded slices,
          searches, and sub-inferences. Frames recurse and fan out through
          <code>rlm-map</code>, returning validated data instead of prose when
          you give them a JSON Schema contract.
        </p>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:1em">
          Calls, tokens, and recursion depth come out of one shared budget, so a
          fan-out cannot outspend its allocation, and the private frame
          conversations cannot pollute yours or your prompt cache.
        </p>

        <div class="meters" id="meters">
          <div>
            <div class="meter__top"><span>Calls</span><b>32</b></div>
            <div class="meter__bar"><i data-fill="100"></i></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="meter__top"><span>Tokens</span><b>400 000</b></div>
            <div class="meter__bar"><i data-fill="78"></i></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="meter__top"><span>Depth</span><b>2</b></div>
            <div class="meter__bar"><i data-fill="50"></i></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="facts" data-rv>
      <div><dt>Corpus</dt><dd>3.1 MB — 121 <code>src/*.lisp</code> files concatenated. <small>Larger than the context window. Never read directly.</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Root conversation</dt><dd>59.6 K tokens <small>(58.7 K input + 915 output). The corpus itself never enters a prompt.</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Wall time</dt><dd>3 min 15 s for the answer <small>· 4 min 36 s for the whole session</small></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Artifact</dt><dd>All 83 condition classes, grouped by 14 subsystems, each with its defining file.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Trace</dt><dd><code>inference:s2Wb1o2</code> <small>— the complete frame conversation, readable in-session with <code>resource.read</code>.</small></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========================================================= sessions -->
<section class="band band--paper" id="sessions">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="label label--accent">05 — Recorded sessions</p>
      <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Real terminals. <em>Nothing sped up.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede head__lede" data-rv>Recorded against v0.35.0 · gpt-5.6-terra (effort high). Each recording loads on demand.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="demos" data-rv>
      <div class="demos__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Recorded sessions">
        <button role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-demo="oversized">Oversized context</button>
        <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-demo="mutation">Break and recover</button>
        <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-demo="continuity">Persist and resume</button>
      </div>

      <div class="demo" role="tabpanel" data-panel="oversized">
        <div class="player" data-cast="casts/oversized-context.cast" data-cols="120" data-rows="34">
          <div class="player__poster">
            <pre>  :::.      :::        AUTOLITH v0.35.0
  ;;`;;     ;;;        ─────────────────────────────────
 ,[[ '[[,   [[[        model      gpt-5.6-terra
c$$$cc$$$c  $$'        workspace  /root/common-lisp/frob/
 888   888,o88oo,.__
 YMM   ""` """"YUMMM</pre>
            <button class="player__load">Load the recording · 4 min 36 s</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <dl class="demo__meta">
          <dt>Prompt</dt><dd>Use <code>rlm.complete</code> over <code>autolith-source.txt</code> in the workspace root. It is the concatenation of this repository's 121 <code>src/*.lisp</code> files, about 3.1 MB, larger than your context window. List every condition class defined in the source, grouped by subsystem, with the defining file for each. Budget of 32 calls, 400 000 tokens, depth 2. Do not read or search the file directly.</dd>
          <dt>Tokens</dt><dd><b>59.6 K</b> in the root conversation. The corpus itself never enters a prompt.</dd>
          <dt>Artifact</dt><dd>All <b>83</b> condition classes across <b>14</b> subsystems, each with its defining file.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="demo" role="tabpanel" data-panel="mutation" hidden>
        <div class="player" data-cast="casts/live-mutation.cast" data-cols="120" data-rows="34">
          <div class="player__poster">
            <pre>  :::.      :::        AUTOLITH v0.35.0
  ;;`;;     ;;;        ─────────────────────────────────
 ,[[ '[[,   [[[        model      gpt-5.6-terra
c$$$cc$$$c  $$'        workspace  /root/common-lisp/frob/
 888   888,o88oo,.__
 YMM   ""` """"YUMMM</pre>
            <button class="player__load">Load the recording · 6 min 19 s</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <dl class="demo__meta">
          <dt>Prompt</dt><dd>Show the source of <code>terminal-ui--duration-text</code> in your running image, redefine it live so durations over 24 hours render as <code>Dd H:MM:SS</code>, exercise it, commit the mutation. Then deliberately break the function, demonstrate the failure, and recover by discarding the broken mutation.</dd>
          <dt>What happened</dt><dd>The break killed the active process outright. Autolith wrote crash capsule <b>efa6aa16</b>, booted the pristine recovery image, restarted from clean committed source with the private commit selected, restored the conversation, and opened a read-only diagnosis turn.</dd>
          <dt>Tokens</dt><dd><b>289.0 K</b> total, most of it the bounded crash context of the diagnosis turn.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="demo" role="tabpanel" data-panel="continuity" hidden>
        <div class="player" data-cast="casts/continuity.cast" data-cols="120" data-rows="34">
          <div class="player__poster">
            <pre>root@lho-thinkpad: ~/common-lisp/frob # ./bin/autolith
  :::.      :::        AUTOLITH v0.35.0
  ;;`;;     ;;;        ─────────────────────────────────
 ,[[ '[[,   [[[        model      gpt-5.6-terra
c$$$cc$$$c  $$'        workspace  /root/common-lisp/frob/
 888   888,o88oo,.__</pre>
            <button class="player__load">Load the recording · 10 min 11 s</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <dl class="demo__meta">
          <dt>Prompt</dt><dd>Define <code>autolith-demo-parse-fraction</code>, exercise it, persist it as a private image commit, add an agenda entry. Then <code>(quit)</code>, <code>autolith resume</code>, and: where were we?</dd>
          <dt>Artifact</dt><dd>Private image commits <b>4048480f</b> and <b>9eee3ae4</b>. The function defined before <code>(quit)</code> answers in the next process without any reloading; the agenda entry written in the first session is found, finished, and marked done in the second.</dd>
          <dt>Wall time</dt><dd><b>10 min 11 s</b> across two processes. Each persist runs the full validation suite before anything is retained.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ state -->
<section class="band band--paper band--tight" id="state" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="head" style="margin-bottom:clamp(2rem,5vh,3rem)">
      <div class="head__top"><p class="label label--accent">06 — Persistent surfaces</p><p class="label">Reconstruction evidence</p></div>
      <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Different kinds of state stay <em>separate.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede head__lede" data-rv>
        Source, conversations, useful facts, live mutations, exact heaps, and
        disposable experiments have different lifetimes. Autolith keeps them
        apart instead of pretending that one database or one saved core is
        everything.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento" data-rv>
      <div class="cell cell--6"><span class="cell__n">01</span><h3 class="display">Conversations</h3><p>Append-only portable S-expressions with exact resume commands, crash-tail repair, and read-only replay navigation.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--3"><span class="cell__n">02</span><h3 class="display">Memories</h3><p>Workspace or global facts, preferences, and decisions with bounded prompt recall.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--3"><span class="cell__n">03</span><h3 class="display">Agendas</h3><p>Short workspace tasks and notes, available in full on every request.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--4"><span class="cell__n">04</span><h3 class="display">Private image commits</h3><p>Complete replay scripts for durable user-specific definitions and settings, retained in private Git.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--4"><span class="cell__n">05</span><h3 class="display">Generations</h3><p>A saved active core, exact tracked source commit, reconstruction script, manifest, and journal position.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--4"><span class="cell__n">06</span><h3 class="display">Worker images</h3><p>Immutable experimental SBCL cores with parentage and durable notes, never selected as the active agent.</p></div>
      <div class="cell cell--12"><span class="cell__n">07</span><h3 class="display">Recovery</h3><p style="max-width:70ch">A separately built pristine image that can inspect a crash and select a known-working generation without loading the damaged core. Shared state transactions are serialized across processes, so concurrent agents can share one workspace.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========================================================== process -->
<section class="band band--ink" id="process">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="proc">
      <div class="stack-3">
        <p class="label label--accent">07 — One process</p>
        <h2 class="display d2" data-split>The agent and its tools run in <em>one image.</em></h2>
        <p class="prose">
          Autolith is a terminal programming agent, not a wrapper around another
          agent process. Its Common Lisp image contains the provider client,
          terminal interface, tool registry, MCP connections, conversation
          state, persistent memories, workspace agenda, and the code that
          decides what happens next.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          If you want inspection without active-image changes, start it with
          <code>--immutable</code>. The mode retains read-only inspection and
          recovery information while withholding evaluation, mutation,
          persistence, checkpoint, and rollback tools.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          Autolith is not a fullscreen TUI. It defers to the base sixteen colors
          your terminal sets, emits prompt markers so your terminal can jump
          between messages, and edits with
          <a class="ulink" href="https://github.com/luciusmagn/clinedi">clinedi</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="imagebox shadowband" id="imagebox" data-rv="fade">
        <div class="imagebox__t"><span>SBCL image</span><span>pid 1</span></div>
        <div class="imagebox__grid">
          <i>provider<br>client</i><i>terminal<br>interface</i><i>tool<br>registry</i>
          <i>MCP<br>connections</i><i>conversation<br>store</i><i>persistent<br>memories</i>
          <i>workspace<br>agenda</i><i>mutation<br>journal</i><i>what happens<br>next</i>
        </div>
        <p class="imagebox__foot">no subprocess boundary between any two of these</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========================================================== install -->
<section class="band band--paper" id="install">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="label label--accent">08 — Install</p>
      <h2 class="display d2" data-split>Binary, Nix, or <em>source.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede head__lede" data-rv>
        The binary carries its own SBCL, Lisp dependencies, and native helpers.
        Installed releases check for newer tags and ask before updating.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="two" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="stack-3">
        <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Install methods">
          <button role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="nix">Nix · recommended</button>
          <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="binary">Binary</button>
          <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="source">Source</button>
          <button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="windows">Windows</button>
        </div>

        <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-tabpanel="nix">
          <div class="shellblock"><span class="p">$</span> nix run github:lambda-symbolics/autolith</div>
          <p class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:.95rem">Nix supplies the complete runtime. This is the better installation path.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-tabpanel="binary" hidden>
          <div class="install">
            <code id="installCmd">curl -fsSL https://sh.lambda-symbolics.com/autolith | sh</code>
            <button class="install__copy" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://sh.lambda-symbolics.com/autolith | sh">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <p class="install__note">Installs or updates the packaged release for your platform.</p>
          <div class="shellblock" style="margin-top:1rem"><span class="p">$</span> autolith</div>
        </div>

        <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-tabpanel="source" hidden>
          <div class="shellblock"><span class="p">$</span> git clone https://github.com/lambda-symbolics/autolith
<span class="p">$</span> cd autolith
<span class="p">$</span> ./script/bootstrap
<span class="p">$</span> ./script/check
<span class="p">$</span> ./bin/autolith</div>
        </div>

        <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-tabpanel="windows" hidden>
          <div class="shellblock"><span class="c">> </span>git clone https://github.com/lambda-symbolics/autolith
<span class="c">> </span>cd autolith
<span class="c">> </span>script\bootstrap.ps1
<span class="c">> </span>bin\autolith.cmd</div>
          <p class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:.95rem">Windows x86_64 runs from a source checkout. See the guide.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="stack-2" style="margin-top:clamp(1.6rem,4vh,2.4rem)">
          <p class="label">Then authenticate a provider</p>
          <div class="shellblock"><span class="p">$</span> autolith auth anthropic   <span class="c">; or chatgpt, gemini, grok, nous,</span>
<span class="p">$</span> autolith                   <span class="c">; fireworks, opencode, openrouter, mistral</span></div>
          <ul class="providers" aria-label="Providers">
            <li>anthropic</li><li>chatgpt</li><li>gemini</li><li>grok</li><li>nous</li><li>fireworks</li><li>opencode</li><li>openrouter</li><li>mistral</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-3">
        <p class="label">Platforms</p>
        <ul class="platforms">
          <li>Linux x86_64</li><li>Linux aarch64</li><li>macOS x86_64</li><li>macOS aarch64</li><li>FreeBSD x86_64</li><li>NetBSD x86_64</li><li>OpenBSD x86_64</li><li>Windows x86_64 · source</li>
        </ul>

        <div style="margin-top:clamp(1.4rem,3vh,2rem)">
          <p class="warn warn--note">Yes, piping a URL into a shell is evil. Read the installer before running it. Nix is the better installation path.</p>
          <p class="warn">Autolith executes model-generated code with your user privileges. Its process boundaries protect reliability, not against hostile code. Use it as a development agent, not as a security sandbox.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="term term--paper" style="margin-top:clamp(1.4rem,3vh,2rem)">
          <div class="term__bar"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>keeping current</span></div>
          <div class="term__body"><pre>(<span style="color:var(--ember-deep)">update</span>)              <span class="c-dim">;; from inside</span>
<span style="color:var(--ember-deep)">$</span> autolith update    <span class="c-dim">;; from the shell</span></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================= cta -->
<section class="band band--ink band--tight">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide" style="text-align:center;display:grid;gap:clamp(1.4rem,3.5vh,2.4rem);justify-items:center">
    <h2 class="display d2" data-split style="max-width:20ch">It is not a small game engine. It is <em>pretty close to a Lisp machine.</em></h2>
    <div class="install" style="margin-inline:auto">
      <code>curl -fsSL https://sh.lambda-symbolics.com/autolith | sh</code>
      <button class="install__copy" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://sh.lambda-symbolics.com/autolith | sh">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__acts" style="justify-content:center">
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/lambda-symbolics/autolith"><span>Read the source</span><span class="btn__arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://zulip.lambda-symbolics.com"><span>Join the Zulip</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>

